        "target_title": "chore: implement many rumdl rules in project",
        "created_at": "2026-10-26T04:35:47.455Z",
        "note": {
          "id": 4087542584,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Enabling `MD029` (ol-prefix) here may conflict with this project's deliberate choice to disable the equivalent markdownlint rule. `.markdownlint-cli2.yaml` turns off `ol-prefix` with the comment \"Disable this rule in the CLI project, because 1. 1. 1. 1. numbering is rendered verbatim in CLI output\", meaning some docs intentionally use all-`1.` ordered lists that markdownlint's default `ol-prefix` style would otherwise flag. `rumdl`'s `MD029` is enabled here with no style override, so if its default disagrees with markdownlint's relaxed handling, CI could start failing on the very lists markdownlint was configured to allow. Did you confirm `rumdl`'s default `MD029` style tolerates the all-`1.` numbering used elsewhere in the docs, or should this rule carry a style override (or be left disabled) to match the markdownlint exception?",
          "author": {
            "id": 21826781,
            "username": "GitLabDuo",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "GitLab Duo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/21826781/duo-bot.png?v=1792265836",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/GitLabDuo"
          },
